Description: A razor-sharp Markdown document reader
 Backtick is an uncompromisingly minimal desktop utility built for
 developers, writers, and technical readers who need a fast, standalone
 way to view .md files without spinning up a heavy IDE or a
 resource-hogging Electron wrapper.
 .
 Built on Tauri, Backtick pairs a high-performance Rust backend with
 the operating system's native Webview rendering engine, resulting in
 a tiny binary size, near-zero RAM footprint, and instant startup.
 .
 Features:
  - Syntax highlighting for code blocks
  - Mermaid diagram rendering
  - Dark mode with Ubuntu-inspired color scheme
  - File associations and context menu integration
  - 100% offline, no analytics, MIT licensed
